WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.524
A support engineer
has to share a screenshot of a ticket,

00:00:03.524 --> 00:00:06.799
and it shows an email,
a phone number and a deploy token.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:11.713
SnapShackle covers them before the picture
leaves, and keeps the evidence.

00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:15.642
Everything on screen is invented,
and this is an expanding prototype.

00:00:15.892 --> 00:00:17.592
Here is how it works.

00:00:17.592 --> 00:00:22.461
It all runs on this one computer:
double-click the launcher and a PowerShell

00:00:22.461 --> 00:00:25.728
host on loopback
serves the studio to your browser.

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:29.720
Captures and settings
stay in one local folder:

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:32.240
a PNG, and a small record beside it.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.636
What goes in is pixels from this PC:

00:00:35.636 --> 00:00:40.000
a region, a window or a screen,
or an image you open or drop in.
